w: There | is a green hill | far a-way, With- | out a cit-y | wall, _ Where | the dear Lord was | cru-ci-fied, Who | died _ to save us | all. _ O | dear-ly, dear-ly, | has He loved, And | we must love Him | too, _ And | trust in His re- | deem-ing blood, And | try * His works to | do. _
